.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-registry-import - Import an image from another registry


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container registry import  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Import an image from another registry

.PP
Copies an image (e.g. \fBnginx:1.27\fR, \fBdocker.io/library/redis:7\fR, \fBghcr.io/gyro-ornek/uygulama:1.0\fR) into the environment's Gyro registry without \fBdocker push\fR\&. HTTPS registries only; only the linux/amd64 variant of multi-platform images is copied. \fBrepo\fR (default: last part of the source name) and \fBtag\fR (default: source tag) name the copy under \fB<host>/<code>/\fR; an existing name:tag needs \fBoverwrite: true\fR\&. Private images: \fBusername\fR + \fBpassword\fR (token) are used only for this copy, never stored or returned, and redacted in the API log. Runs in the background: poll GET .../registry/imports. Limits: 1 running import per environment (409 \fBimport_running\fR), 10 per hour (429 \fBimport_rate_limited\fR), 15 minutes, 128 layers, size within the free registry space (50 GB cap, 2 GB free, then the usual €0.05/GB-month). Sources that resolve to private, internal or Gyro infrastructure addresses are refused (\fBsource_blocked\fR).

.PP
API: POST /cloud/containers/{id}/registry/imports (operationId importContainerImage, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for import

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--overwrite\fP[=false]
	replace an existing name:tag

.PP
\fB--password\fP=""
	private source: token / password (not stored, redacted in logs)

.PP
\fB--repo\fP=""
	target name under your prefix (lowercase, max 3 levels)

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--source\fP=""
	source image (host/repo:tag or @sha256:...); docker.io when no host

.PP
\fB--tag\fP=""
	target tag (default: source tag, \fBlatest\fR for a digest)

.PP
\fB--username\fP=""
	private source: username (not stored)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
